[[:db/retract 17592186198562 :question/answer-fields 17592186194003] {:db/id 17592186198562 :question/problem "The maximum value of the quadratic form $Q(x)=-{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2},$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to $3.$ Which of the following is a vector $x$ at which the maximum is attained?" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n \nThe maximum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-3I & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-3I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{max}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-72e392f4-71c8-5797-8085-77f0d25ff7b9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-72e392f4-71c8-5797-8085-77f0d25ff7b9" :answer-field/id #uuid "72e392f4-71c8-5797-8085-77f0d25ff7b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1512bf0f-a0b6-5737-8456-15bf7348d13a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b75669b6-5915-5577-8d99-85ede9b169dc" "answer-e53e0f0c-01ad-5114-93c5-0442b0a0663a" "answer-3cba96ef-b9b9-582c-9ce3-fb19b45e7859" "answer-1512bf0f-a0b6-5737-8456-15bf7348d13a" "answer-189d044b-20ef-594f-9050-30d36ea1c805"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b75669b6-5915-5577-8d99-85ede9b169dc" :answer/id #uuid "b75669b6-5915-5577-8d99-85ede9b169dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e53e0f0c-01ad-5114-93c5-0442b0a0663a" :answer/id #uuid "e53e0f0c-01ad-5114-93c5-0442b0a0663a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cba96ef-b9b9-582c-9ce3-fb19b45e7859" :answer/id #uuid "3cba96ef-b9b9-582c-9ce3-fb19b45e7859" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1512bf0f-a0b6-5737-8456-15bf7348d13a" :answer/id #uuid "1512bf0f-a0b6-5737-8456-15bf7348d13a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-189d044b-20ef-594f-9050-30d36ea1c805" :answer/id #uuid "189d044b-20ef-594f-9050-30d36ea1c805" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-dc255669-05a8-5b16-b22c-2690d4b2f343" :activity/id #uuid "dc255669-05a8-5b16-b22c-2690d4b2f343" :activity/title "Constrained Optimization of Quadratic Forms: Determining Where Extrema are Attained" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048933 :activity/